Fixes two issues.
- Calling `addPaths` would erroneously fire the directoryChanged signal some short amount of time after the call.
  - This was caused by checkDir including hidden files, while scanForDirEntries did not.
- Moving a file into a watched folder via Finder would cause the signal to fire twice.
  - Finder moves the file into the directory first, then updates .DS_Store afterwards, triggering the event twice.
  - Fixed by moving the isSameTimestampAndMode check to the else block. When the .DS_Store change occurs, the directory keeps the same timestamp and mode, so dirChanged itself no longer gets set to true, meaning the signal is not re-fired.

